[[File:Aquanite icon.png|left]]
'''[[Aquanite|Aquanites]]''' are Slayer monsters found in the [[Ynysdail Cavern]] beneath [[Ynysdail]]. They require level 78 [[Slayer]] to fight, and accessing Ynysdail itself requires 73 [[Sailing]] and a boat equipped with an [[adamant keel]] or better. 

Aquanites can be killed normally and [[Mortimer]] can assign them as a Slayer task by default; however, to receive them as a Slayer task from [[Nieve]] or [[Duradel]], players must first unlock them for 80 [[Slayer reward points]]. A task extension is also available for 100 points.
Aquanites can drop the unique [[Aquanite tendon]], used to make the [[Aquanite hopper]]. 

Accessing [[Ynysdail]] requires the player to enter the crystalline maze from the outside, or build the rowboat hotspot on the island. This rowboat, once built, will generate another one north of [[Gwenith]]. Using this rowboat requires completion of [[Song of the Elves]]. It is recommended to complete the quest to avoid having to set the ship back to a [[mooring point]] if a [[Greater teleport focus (facility)|greater teleport focus]] is not on it.

While on an Aquanite slayer task, there is a 1/200 chance (1/150 with completion of the [[Combat Achievements/Elite|elite tier of Combat Achievements]]) for an [[Elder Aquanite]] to spawn after killing an Aquanite, provided the player has the ''Bigger and Badder'' unlock. Elder Aquanites have a special attack that will deal 50 damage if [[Protect from Magic]] has been active for some time, so flicking the prayer on and off between the enemy's attacks is required to avoid taking damage. 

Aquanites attack with Magic and have high accuracy, so using [[Protect from Magic]] is highly recommended. Alternatively, they can be safespotted with a 9 or 10 tile attack range. They are located in a [[single-way combat]] area, and a [[Dwarf multicannon]] cannot be used as the ground is too damp to place one.

When hit with a slash attack, an Aquanite’s lure will be severed, reducing its stab Defence by 50 (from 60 to 10). This greatly improves the accuracy of subsequent stab attacks and is especially helpful for players with lower [[Attack]] levels. Because dealing damage is not required to sever the lure, a fast 4-tick slash weapon such as a [[Scimitar]] or [[Abyssal whip]] is recommended. The [[Saradomin godsword]]'s special attack can also be used if no other special attack weapons are brought along. Alternatively, a weapon that has both attack styles may be used, such as the [[Ghrazi rapier]], while swapping between slash and stab styles.

[[File:Aquanite safespot.png|left|thumb|Tiles that can be used to safespot Aquanites with a longrange weapon]]

==Recommended skills==
*When killing '''Aquanites''' with Ranged, the following skill levels are recommended:
**{{SCP|Ranged|80+}}
**{{SCP|Prayer|63}} for [[Deadeye]] or 74 for [[Rigour]]

*When killing '''Aquanites''' with Melee, the following skill levels are recommended:
**{{SCP|Attack|80+}}
**{{SCP|Strength|80+}}
**{{SCP|Prayer|70}} for [[Piety]]

== Getting to Ynysdail ==
=== First-time access ===
The first time traveling to [[Ynysdail]], you must sail there manually, using a boat equipped with an [[adamant keel]] or better. Upon arrival on the island, the player can build a rowboat. After building the rowboat, players can travel freely between Ynysdail and Gwenith. 

=== Constructing the rowboat ===
70 [[Construction]] is needed to construct the rowboat.  
This requires the following materials:

{{Checklist|
*1 [[Hammer]]
*1 [[Saw]]
*10 [[Swamp paste]]
*8 [[Camphor plank]]
}}

